  "laws": [
    "This is a finite fictional object-logic campaign, not real Mars engineering. All recipes, parts, compatibility conditions, map geometry, phase rows and goal requirements are public.",
    "Known concepts and learned assembly designs are inexhaustible. There are no item quantities, fuel, oxygen budget, stored water, battery charge, production rates, move quotas or depletion timers.",
    "The player combines named ingredients or actual world objects/places. No action delegates construction of a requested finished output. A whole known assembly can be reused directly.",
    "Assembly recipes retain real component trees. Other legal attachments and containments can make unnamed larger assemblies. Properties arise from actual parts and relationships, not the name of a result.",
    "Transformation recipes replace one actual local material surface with declared output properties and retain immutable input provenance. An ingredient’s ancestral properties are not output capabilities. Actual working heat, water, form and record contexts are required where declared; retained tools and sources are not consumed.",
    "Local surface tests require all named traits on that same actual part. A frame and clear film are not one rigid clear surface. Active-boundary requirements check the specified contained leaves, not an unrelated decorative panel. Diffuse boundaries pass growing light but not faithful images.",
    "Profiles are public finite tuples of opening, contact edges and facing. Actual fit combines a material at a place with that place’s matching profile and records its then-current traits. A copied profile may fit too, but does not acquire the original’s impression or earlier soft-fit event.",
    "Copies have independent physical identities and preserve their saved geometry and interfaces. A copy does not acquire another object’s observation events, sample history, achievements, movement history or external connections.",
    "Clear enclosing film protects an actual interior while transmitting light. Reflective foil blocks transmitted light and can redirect a real beam according to public facing. Mesh screens dust without making a place dark. Covering affects actual containment, not every object sharing a place.",
    "A real solar cell supplies its attached or connected powered parts when it faces the row’s sun and is exposed, or when real connected light reaches it. Aiming a whole object also aims its parts; targeting an actual part can aim that part independently. Light, power, warmth and water are boolean effects with source provenance, not counted stock. Shading the actual cell removes its supply. A source-free lamp–solar loop supplies nothing.",
    "Sources recur inexhaustibly. Warmth applied to an actual ice face permits water there. A still or filtered passage separates the dirty-water tag. A rootbed grows only with the required actual enclosure, light and clean-water contact.",
    "A wheel-bearing supported assembly moves as the same object, carrying actual parts and records. Paths, low arches, width and deployed spans determine fit. Traversing several empty edges is one movement choice, not several counted turns.",
    "Hinges expose explicit poses. A span supports an actual gap only while a compatible physical span remains there. Moving the only supporting object away cannot leave an imaginary bridge.",
    "Cameras acquire records only through actual illuminated visible subjects at actual viewpoints. Sample supports acquire site tags only through contact with actual specimen places. Sending a record requires an actual optical event and the receiver retains what really arrived.",
    "A wet place exposes its surfaces to water; actual watertight surfaces or actual enclosing protection provide dryness. A named alcove never protects an object automatically. No fluid quantity, loss timer or damage counter is modeled.",
    "Goal modes are public: current services must all be true together at the campaign endpoint; an explicit achievement is a completed lifecycle stage that stays earned after a legitimate later change. Every card also reports its current truth and first achievement separately.",
    "Exposure rows are fixed, public test conditions, not advancing weather or hidden timers. The engine checks all required rows automatically. Inspecting or waiting for a row is not construction work.",
    "There are thirty finite goal cards on ten retained maps. Goals inspect resulting properties, identities and actual events rather than an exact recipe or a required move count. A single combine may satisfy two cards; count it once.",
    "Known designs transfer across maps; each map retains its own physical state and pauses when inactive. Navigation, inspections, previews, assembly selection, automatic checks and reports are not counted combines.",
    "A shorter valid answer is a complete answer. Full catalogue and whole-assembly shortcuts remain legal. Comfortable clear steps are allowed, but repeated no-op commands, forced repairs and manual duplication do not manufacture campaign length.",
    "Surface traits belong to each actual local part, not the union of its ancestral inputs. Transformation replaces that leaf; its tools stay. Immutable provenance describes inputs and genuine sources but grants no capabilities.",
    "A supported closed boundary may use clear, diffuse, reflecting, opaque, porous or watertight local surfaces. Watertight boundaries enclose; porous mesh-like boundaries protect from dust without sealing. The stored local profile face/edges describe template fit; optical aim changes beam facing, not that imprinted tuple. A diffuse boundary admits light but not a faithful camera view; reflecting/opaque boundaries block both. A named protected place does not cover objects.",
    "Only attached surfaces form a skin; an outside surface stays exterior and does not become an enclosure around existing interior contents. A rigid material can support its own attached boundary. A frame supports other boundaries. Surface goal tests refer to the SAME local part for all listed traits and contact edges, never a trait union across parts. encloses means that exact surface actively bounds the listed inside contents.",
    "An exposed porous open-profile material separates incoming dirty water when used in a water-bearing assembly. Lining it makes it watertight and stops that local filter route; independent other filters still work. Water links still need a tube endpoint. No volume or stock exists.",
    "Profile opening, named contact edges and face are a finite local fit tuple. fit requires exact equality at the actual place and records current traits without changing them. take-form copies an actual template tuple and records a real impression. Structural copies may retain geometry but NEVER impression, fit, optical or specimen events.",
    "Wet places penetrate un-enclosed porous surfaces; watertight surfaces remain locally dry. Temporary porous records are not usable there until protected; history is retained, not destroyed. Durable watertight recording surfaces remain usable. Surface dry/protected tests use the actual boundary, not every object sharing its place.",
    "Records are bound to actual carrier parts. Appending a blank plate does not transfer a wet sheet’s records; actual optical relay to a receiving plate does. Initial component origins survive actual assembly and transformations but are scrubbed on design copies. Optical records retain actual faithful lens identities and view-boundary IDs and local trait/form snapshots. A throughSurface goal binds its current boundary to that same genuine observation; adding a later clear coating cannot retroactively change an earlier view. All exposure rows are simultaneous test conditions, not elapsed turns. Goal mode current must be true together at the campaign endpoint; achievement goals preserve explicitly stated lifecycle accomplishment. firstIntervention reports historical success separately. No minimum move count or required recipe list exists."
  ],
  "operations": {
    "transform": "operation transform: select material (known or actual) as a, catalyst/tool/place as b. recipe optionally selects among matching public rules; part targets ONE local input leaf, toolPart selects an actual template/tool part. Actual operands must touch at the same place. Heat/water/form/record context must actually exist. A new functional leaf replaces only the material; tools remain. Known abstract film/foil/mesh/binder can be copied as inexhaustible tools.",
    "fit": "operation fit: actual object + current place with public form. context.part selects local surface. Exact opening/contact-edge/face profile required. Records this actual part’s fit and present rigidity; no property or shape is changed. Copies cannot fabricate fit history.",
    "grammar": "{type:\"combine\", a:known-design-or-object-id, b:known-design-or-object-id-or-place:ID, context?:{operation?,at?,channel?,direction?,part?,toolPart?,recipe?,via?}}",
    "default": "Two known operands make an actual assembly and reusable design. A known operand plus place creates a fresh copy. An actual object plus place moves that same object (frame+wheels required except from workbench). Movement context.at or context.via optionally names route waypoints, still one whole trip with no per-edge charge. Actual+known or colocated actual+actual attaches and preserves the first actual host identity.",
    "attach": "Actual host receives the other operand; target a subtree with context.part. inside requires a supported boundary; outside leaves an exterior part. All actual part trees remain inspectable.",
    "connect": "Two actual object IDs, context.channel power/water/light. Needs a public anchor route; power needs endpoint cable, water endpoint tube. Light additionally needs cardinal unobstructed path, facing source, and lamp/reflector/guide. External links detach on travel.",
    "pose": "Object combined with itself: operation aim plus direction rotates all its parts (or only context.part); fold/open/close requires a hinge in selected part. A folded hinged root fits low/narrow routes; folded root boundary is open.",
    "observe": "Actual camera + place, operation observe: lens and plate required; an unobstructed cardinal view and illuminated target in at least one public row produces actual records. All successful rows are recorded automatically; zero waiting.",
    "transmit": "Actual record-bearing object + receiver place or another actual record-plate assembly, operation transmit: cardinal unobstructed path and actual emitted/guided light or an illuminated lens; receiver retains the original record IDs. For an actual recipient, context.part may select its receiving record plate; freshness is checked on that physical plate, so a real relay may transfer a record already present only on another unreadable carrier.",
    "sample": "Actual tray+plate object + its current specimen place, operation sample: actual contact is retained, never copied into a design.",
    "span": "Actual unfolded frame object at one gap endpoint + opposite endpoint place, operation span: supports that gap until moved/folded. Any fitting object may serve, not only a named bridge.",
    "copy": "Known complete designs are inexhaustible. Copies retain part arrangement/pose/facing; new identities, no samples/records/history and no automatically fitted external links. Automatic internal conduction is structural.",
    "undo": "Physical pre-state restored; learned knowledge/designs, current map, and identity serial floor retained. Capture cumulative accepted action count is never erased. Undo and queries count zero."
  }
}

